# Question 3 -- Update Image and Watch RollingUpdate

## Objective

Change the Nginx image and observe Kubernetes perform a RollingUpdate.

Check current image:

``` bash
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment \
  -o=jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}'
```

Watch Pods:

``` bash
kubectl get pods -w
```

In another terminal:

``` bash
kubectl set image deployment nginx-deployment nginx=nginx:1.27
```

Check rollout:

``` bash
kubectl rollout status deployment nginx-deployment
```

Check ReplicaSets:

``` bash
kubectl get rs
```

Verify final image:

``` bash
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment \
  -o=jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}'
```

## Expected flow

``` text
Deployment
    |
    +--> Old ReplicaSet
    |
    +--> New ReplicaSet
              |
              +--> New Pods
```

The new ReplicaSet is scaled up while the old ReplicaSet is scaled down.

