# Question 4 -- Configure maxSurge and maxUnavailable

## Objective

Explicitly configure RollingUpdate behavior and understand the Pod
limits during an update.

Use:

``` yaml
spec:
  replicas: 4

  strategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      maxSurge: 1
      maxUnavailable: 1
```

Full relevant section:

``` yaml
spec:
  replicas: 4
  strategy:
    type: RollingUpdate
    rollingUpdate:
      maxSurge: 1
      maxUnavailable: 1
```

Apply:

``` bash
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
```

Verify:

``` bash
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment
```

Check configuration:

``` bash
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -o yaml | grep -A5 rollingUpdate
```

Watch Pods:

``` bash
kubectl get pods -w
```

Trigger update:

``` bash
kubectl set image deployment nginx-deployment nginx=nginx:1.27
```

Check rollout:

``` bash
kubectl rollout status deployment nginx-deployment
```

## With 4 replicas

``` text
Desired replicas = 4
maxSurge = 1
Maximum Pods = 5

maxUnavailable = 1
Minimum available = 3
```

## Key learning

``` text
maxSurge       = extra Pods allowed
maxUnavailable = unavailable Pods allowed
```

The exact observed sequence can be fast and may not visibly show all
intermediate states.

